\]

\[
m_p = 1.67\times10^{-27}\ {\rm kg}
\]

\[
N = \frac{31\ {\rm kg}}{1.67\times10^{-27}\ {\rm kg/proton}}
   \approx 1.85\times10^{28}\ \text{protons}
\]

The decay constant is

\[
\lambda = \frac{\ln 2}{T_{1/2}} ,
\qquad T_{1/2}=10^{33}\ \text{yr}=10^{33}\times365.25\ \text{days}
            \approx 3.65\times10^{35}\ \text{days}
\]

\[
\lambda = \frac{0.693}{3.65\times10^{35}}\ \text{day}^{-1}
        \approx 1.9\times10^{-36}\ \text{day}^{-1}
\]

Expected decays per day:

\[
R = N\lambda \approx (1.85\times10^{28})(1.9\times10^{-36})
    \approx 3.5\times10^{-8}\ \text{decays/day}
\]

Thus the number of proton decays per day from the body is \( \approx 3.5\times10^{-8}\).

